{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string the given number of times.\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\n\"\"\"\ndef odd_Equivalent(s, n):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of odd numbers when rotating binary string s for n rotations.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        rotated = s[i:] + s[:i]\n        if int(rotated, 2) % 2 == 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the next smallest palindrome of a specified integer, returned as an integer.\nassert next_smallest_palindrome(99)==101\n\"\"\"\ndef next_smallest_palindrome(n):\n    # Convert to string and find the next palindrome greater than n\n    s = str(n + 1)\n    length = len(s)\n    \n    while True:\n        # Check if current number is palindrome\n        if s == s[::-1]:\n            return int(s)\n        \n        # Make it palindrome by mirroring left half to right half\n        mid = length // 2\n        left_half = s[:mid]\n        \n        if length % 2 == 0:\n            # Even length\n            candidate = left_half + left_half[::-1]\n        else:\n            # Odd length\n            candidate = left_half + s[mid] + left_half[::-1]\n        \n        # If candidate > original string, we found our answer\n        if candidate > s:\n            return int(candidate)\n        \n        # Otherwise, increment the middle part and try again\n        if length % 2 == 0:\n            left_num = int(left_half)\n            left_num += 1\n            left_str = str(left_num)\n            if len(left_str) > len(left_half):\n                # Carry over, need longer palindrome\n                return int('1' + '0' * (length - 1) + '1')\n            left_str = left_str.zfill(len(left_half))\n            s = left_str + left_str[::-1]\n        else:\n            left_num = int(left_half)\n            mid_char = s[mid]\n            mid_num = int(mid_char)\n            \n            if mid_num < 9:\n                s = left_half + str(mid_num + 1) + left_half[::-1]\n            else:\n                left_num += 1\n                left_str = str(left_num)\n                if len(left_str) > len(left_half):\n                    return int('1' + '0' * (length - 1) + '1')\n                left_str = left_str.zfill(len(left_half))\n                s = left_str + '0' + left_str[::-1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string the given number of times.\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\n\"\"\"\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_str, rotations):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of numbers with odd values when rotating binary string.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(rotations):\n        rotated = binary_str[i:] + binary_str[:i]\n        decimal_value = int(rotated, 2)\n        if decimal_value % 2 == 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
