{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array which is formed by repeating the given array k times.\nassert max_sub_array_sum_repeated([10, 20, -30, -1], 4, 3) == 30\n\"\"\"\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    \"\"\"Find the largest sum of contiguous subarray in array repeated k times.\"\"\"\n    if k == 1:\n        max_ending_here = max_so_far = arr[0]\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            max_ending_here = max(arr[i], max_ending_here + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n        return max_so_far\n    \n    # Calculate max subarray sum for single array\n    max_kadane = float('-inf')\n    curr_max = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        curr_max = max(arr[i], curr_max + arr[i])\n        max_kadane = max(max_kadane, curr_max)\n    \n    # Calculate prefix and suffix sums\n    prefix_sum = float('-inf')\n    curr_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        curr_sum += arr[i]\n        prefix_sum = max(prefix_sum, curr_sum)\n    \n    suffix_sum = float('-inf')\n    curr_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        curr_sum += arr[i]\n        suffix_sum = max(suffix_sum, curr_sum)\n    \n    # Total sum of array\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n    \n    # If total sum is positive, we can benefit from middle repetitions\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        return max(max_kadane, prefix_sum + suffix_sum + (k-2) * total_sum)\n    else:\n        return max(max_kadane, prefix_sum + suffix_sum)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the count of all binary sequences of length 2n such that sum of first n bits is same as sum of last n bits.\nassert math.isclose(count_binary_seq(1), 2.0, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\ndef count_binary_seq(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of binary sequences of length 2n where sum of first n bits equals sum of last n bits.\"\"\"\n    from math import comb\n    total = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        total += comb(n, k) * comb(n, k)\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the depth of a dictionary.\nassert dict_depth({'a':1, 'b': {'c': {'d': {}}}})==4\n\"\"\"\ndef dict_depth(d):\n    \"\"\"Returns the maximum depth of a nested dictionary.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(d, dict) or not d:\n        return 1\n    return 1 + max(dict_depth(value) for value in d.values())"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to calculate the maximum aggregate from the list of tuples.\nassert max_aggregate([('Juan Whelan',90),('Sabah Colley',88),('Peter Nichols',7),('Juan Whelan',122),('Sabah Colley',84)])==('Juan Whelan', 212)\n\"\"\"\ndef max_aggregate(tuples_list):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the maximum aggregate from list of tuples by summing values for each name.\"\"\"\n    aggregates = {}\n    for name, value in tuples_list:\n        aggregates[name] = aggregates.get(name, 0) + value\n    return max(aggregates.items(), key=lambda x: x[1])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to calculate the maximum aggregate from the list of tuples.\nassert max_aggregate([('Juan Whelan',90),('Sabah Colley',88),('Peter Nichols',7),('Juan Whelan',122),('Sabah Colley',84)])==('Juan Whelan', 212)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_aggregate(tuples_list):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the maximum aggregate from list of tuples by name.\"\"\"\n    name_totals = {}\n    for name, value in tuples_list:\n        name_totals[name] = name_totals.get(name, 0) + value\n    max_name = max(name_totals, key=name_totals.get)\n    return (max_name, name_totals[max_name])\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the depth of a dictionary.\nassert dict_depth({'a':1, 'b': {'c': {'d': {}}}})==4\n\"\"\"\ndef dict_depth(d):\n    \"\"\"Returns the maximum depth of nested dictionaries.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(d, dict) or not d:\n        return 1\n    return 1 + max(dict_depth(v) for v in d.values())"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to return two words from a list of words starting with letter 'p'.\nassert start_withp([\"Python PHP\", \"Java JavaScript\", \"c c++\"])==('Python', 'PHP')\n\"\"\"\ndef start_withp(lst):\n    \"\"\"Returns two words starting with 'p' from the given list.\"\"\"\n    p_words = []\n    for item in lst:\n        words = item.split()\n        for word in words:\n            if word.lower().startswith('p'):\n                p_words.append(word)\n                if len(p_words) == 2:\n                    return tuple(p_words)\n    return tuple(p_words) if p_words else ()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the count of all binary sequences of length 2n such that sum of first n bits is same as sum of last n bits.\nassert math.isclose(count_binary_seq(1), 2.0, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef count_binary_seq(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of binary sequences of length 2n where sum of first n bits equals sum of last n bits.\"\"\"\n    def nCr(n, r):\n        if r > n or r < 0:\n            return 0\n        if r == 0 or r == n:\n            return 1\n        result = 1\n        for i in range(min(r, n - r)):\n            result = result * (n - i) // (i + 1)\n        return result\n    \n    count = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        count += nCr(n, k) * nCr(n, k)\n    return float(count)\n```"}
