{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the specified number of largest products from two given lists, selecting one factor from each list.\nassert large_product([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6],[3, 6, 8, 9, 10, 6],3)==[60, 54, 50]\n\"\"\"\ndef large_product(nums1, nums2, num):\n    products = []\n    for i in nums1:\n        for j in nums2:\n            products.append(i * j)\n    products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return products[:num]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the specified number of largest products from two given lists, selecting one factor from each list.\nassert large_product([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6],[3, 6, 8, 9, 10, 6],3)==[60, 54, 50]\n\"\"\"\ndef large_product(nums1, nums2, num):\n    # Generate all possible products and sort in descending order\n    products = []\n    for n1 in nums1:\n        for n2 in nums2:\n            products.append(n1 * n2)\n    products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return products[:num]"}
