{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the volume of a cone.\nassert math.isclose(volume_cone(5,12), 314.15926535897927, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef volume_cone(radius, height):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the volume of a cone using the formula V = (1/3) * \u03c0 * r\u00b2 * h.\"\"\"\n    return (1/3) * math.pi * radius**2 * height\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until ith index and also including a given kth element which is after i, i.e., k > i .\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5 ], 7, 4, 6) == 11\n\"\"\"\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find maximum sum of increasing subsequence ending at index i, then including element at index k\n    dp_prefix = [0] * n\n    dp_prefix[0] = arr[0]\n    \n    # Calculate maximum increasing subsequence sum up to each position\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        dp_prefix[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp_prefix[j] = max(dp_prefix[j], dp_prefix[prev] + arr[j])\n    \n    # Find maximum sum ending at or before index i, then add element at index k if valid\n    max_sum_at_i = max(dp_prefix[:i+1])\n    \n    # Check if we can extend with element at index k\n    result = max_sum_at_i\n    for j in range(i+1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            result = max(result, dp_prefix[j] + arr[k])\n    \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the volume of a cone.\nassert math.isclose(volume_cone(5,12), 314.15926535897927, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef volume_cone(radius, height):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the volume of a cone using the formula V = (1/3) * \u03c0 * r\u00b2 * h.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    return (1/3) * math.pi * radius**2 * height\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set the left most unset bit.\nassert set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14\n\"\"\"\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    \"\"\"Set the leftmost unset bit in the binary representation of n.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit\n    temp = n\n    bit_position = 0\n    \n    # Find the highest set bit position\n    while temp:\n        temp >>= 1\n        bit_position += 1\n    \n    # Check each bit from left to right to find first unset bit\n    for i in range(bit_position, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the next higher bit\n    return n | (1 << bit_position)"}
