{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set the left most unset bit.\nassert set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    \"\"\"Set the leftmost unset bit in the binary representation of n.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Find the position of the leftmost set bit\n    temp = n\n    position = 0\n    while temp > 0:\n        temp >>= 1\n        position += 1\n    \n    # Check if the bit at position is already set\n    if n & (1 << position):\n        # If set, set the next bit to the left\n        return n | (1 << position)\n    else:\n        # If not set, set the bit at position\n        return n | (1 << (position - 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the n'th lucas number.\nassert find_lucas(9) == 76\n\"\"\"\ndef find_lucas(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the n'th Lucas number where L(0)=2, L(1)=1.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    a, b = 2, 1\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
