{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to compute the sum of digits of each number of a given list.\nassert sum_of_digits([10,2,56])==14\n\"\"\"\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Compute the sum of digits for each number in the list and return their total.\"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        while num > 0:\n            total += num % 10\n            num //= 10\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum possible by using the given equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\nassert get_max_sum(60) == 106\n\"\"\"\ndef get_max_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns maximum sum using f(n) = max(f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5), n).\"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n    \n    def solve(num):\n        if num in memo:\n            return memo[num]\n        \n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        divided_sum = solve(num // 2) + solve(num // 3) + solve(num // 4) + solve(num // 5)\n        result = max(divided_sum, num)\n        memo[num] = result\n        return result\n    \n    return solve(n)"}
