{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to move all zeroes to the end of the given list.\nassert move_zero([1,0,2,0,3,4]) == [1,2,3,4,0,0]\n\"\"\"\ndef move_zero(lst):\n    \"\"\"Move all zeroes to the end of the list while maintaining order of non-zero elements.\"\"\"\n    non_zero = [x for x in lst if x != 0]\n    zero_count = len(lst) - len(non_zero)\n    return non_zero + [0] * zero_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to move all zeroes to the end of the given list.\nassert move_zero([1,0,2,0,3,4]) == [1,2,3,4,0,0]\n\"\"\"\ndef move_zero(lst):\n    \"\"\"Moves all zeros to the end of the list while maintaining order of non-zero elements.\"\"\"\n    non_zeros = [x for x in lst if x != 0]\n    zeros = [0] * (len(lst) - len(non_zeros))\n    return non_zeros + zeros"}
