{"task_id": "Mbpp/758", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to count lists within a list. The function should return a dictionary where every list is converted to a tuple and the value of such tuple is the number of its occurencies in the original list.\nassert unique_sublists([[1, 3], [5, 7], [1, 3], [13, 15, 17], [5, 7], [9, 11]] )=={(1, 3): 2, (5, 7): 2, (13, 15, 17): 1, (9, 11): 1}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef unique_sublists(lst):\n    \"\"\"Count occurrences of sublists converted to tuples.\"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for sublist in lst:\n        key = tuple(sublist)\n        result[key] = result.get(key, 0) + 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check whether a given string is a decimal number with a precision of 2.\nassert is_decimal('123.11')==True\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef is_decimal(s):\n    \"\"\"Check if string is a decimal number with exactly 2 decimal places.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        parts = s.split('.')\n        if len(parts) != 2:\n            return False\n        int(parts[0]) if parts[0] != '' else 0\n        return len(parts[1]) == 2 and parts[1].isdigit()\n    except (ValueError, AttributeError):\n        return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/758", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to count lists within a list. The function should return a dictionary where every list is converted to a tuple and the value of such tuple is the number of its occurencies in the original list.\nassert unique_sublists([[1, 3], [5, 7], [1, 3], [13, 15, 17], [5, 7], [9, 11]] )=={(1, 3): 2, (5, 7): 2, (13, 15, 17): 1, (9, 11): 1}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef unique_sublists(lists):\n    \"\"\"Count occurrences of sublists by converting them to tuples.\"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for sublist in lists:\n        key = tuple(sublist)\n        result[key] = result.get(key, 0) + 1\n    return result\n```"}
